---
title: Red lentil dal
tags: [indian, vegan]
cuisine: indian
source: Red lentil dal by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/red-lentil-dal
---

> A restaurant batch. The curry oil makes far more than the dal uses; it keeps in the fridge.

== Curry oil ==

In a #large stockpot{} over medium-high heat, bring the @neutral oil{32%cup}, @madras curry powder{2%cup}, @fennel seeds{1/2%cup}(cracked), @garlic{48%cloves}(lightly cracked), @long pepper{40}(lightly cracked), @garlic{32%cloves}(peeled, crushed), @orange peel{16}, @shallots{16}(sliced), @cinnamon sticks{16}(lightly cracked), @ginger{1}(16-inch knob, peeled, crushed) and @cumin seeds{2 1/2%tbsp}(cracked) up to 212°F.

Take off the heat and steep ~{2%hours}. Strain through a #chinois{} lined with a coffee filter, and keep in quart containers in the fridge.

== Dal ==

In a #large stockpot{} over medium heat, put the @shallots{750%g}, @chile oil{100%g}, @ginger{90%g}(sliced), @curry leaves{90%g}, @garlic{36%g}(smashed), @mustard seeds{25%g}, @fennel seeds{28%g}, @black peppercorns{18%g}, @whole cloves{18}, @green cardamom pods{9}, @star anise{3}(pods) and 4 cups of the curry oil. Sweat until fragrant and the curry leaves are glossy.

Add the @red lentils{12%cup}, @madras curry powder{125%g} and @turmeric powder{60%g}. Toast until the lentils turn opaque.

Add about @water{36%cup}(9 quarts) and cook until the lentils are soft. Season with @kosher salt{} and @granulated sugar{}.

Blend smooth with an #immersion blender{}. Taste, adjust the salt and sugar, and serve.
